  "wording": {
    "supported": "Pass on all three systems in this preliminary, unpromoted run. The error of \"supported\" needs no further multiplicity correction (intersection–union).",
    "not supported": "Fail on at least one system. The error of \"not supported\" is not controlled this way (§7), and this is not a statement about systems beyond the three studied.",
    "inconclusive": "No system failed and at least one could not be decided at this precision. Inconclusive does not say the effect is absent.",
    "reading:H2a": "Pre-registered reading of a failure (v3 §7): instability enters the weight through anisotropic seeds, and the size of the departure measures how far real attractors are from the separation assumption.",
    "reading:H2c": "Pre-registered reading (v3 §7), to be applied by the reader from the reported A4o − A2 interval: if H2c fails but A4o beats A2, the theory is right and the deployable seed estimates limit it.",
    "gate_failure": "GATE FAILURE: at least one system failed the validation gate (E0). Its results are PROVISIONAL, its verdicts are shown as computed, and the failure is referred to the owner (DEC-0027, DEC-0031). Nothing proceeds to promotion until the owner rules.",
    "gate_ok": "Every system passed the validation gate, so no result carries the PROVISIONAL mark.",
    "gpu_agree": "Every primary part is within the bound, no verdict-type leaf differs and the GPU gate passed on every system. The cross-check changes no verdict (DEC-0031).",
    "gpu_disagree": "At least one primary part exceeds the bound, a verdict-type leaf differs or a GPU gate failed. This is reported here only and changes no verdict (DEC-0031)."
  },
